WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.601
-Welcome back to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:03.934
It is time to play
"Egg Roulette."

00:00:03.934 --> 00:00:05.601
But I'm going to need some help.
[ Drumroll ]

00:00:05.601 --> 00:00:08.734
He won a Golden Globe for
his portrayal of Elvis Presley

00:00:08.734 --> 00:00:11.067
in the movie "Elvis"
and now he's nominated

00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:13.467
for an Academy Award
for Best Actor.

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:15.868
Please welcome Austin Butler!

00:00:15.868 --> 00:00:17.367
[ Cheers and applause ]
Come on, now!

00:00:17.367 --> 00:00:18.467
♪♪

00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:22.167
-Thank you.
-Come on.

00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:23.901
That's Austin Butler
right there.

00:00:23.901 --> 00:00:25.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:28.801 --> 00:00:31.200
Higgins, would you like to
explain how this works?

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.567
-Yes, James.

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:37.000
Here in my hand,
I have one-dozen eggs.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.267
Eight of them
have been hard-boiled.

00:00:39.267 --> 00:00:41.167
Four of them are still raw.

00:00:41.167 --> 00:00:44.000
You and Austin will take turns
selecting one egg at a time

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.767
and smashing it upon
the top of your head.

00:00:46.767 --> 00:00:51.133
You won't know which eggs are
raw and which are hard-boiled.

00:00:51.133 --> 00:00:53.634
You must choose an egg.
-What?

00:00:53.634 --> 00:00:55.400
-Once you choose it,
no put-backs.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:56.534
You must smash that egg
upon your head.

00:00:56.534 --> 00:00:57.567
-Okay.

00:00:57.567 --> 00:01:00.501
-First one to get
two raw eggs loses.

00:01:00.501 --> 00:01:01.868
Austin, would you like
to go first?

00:01:01.868 --> 00:01:03.400
-You got this, bud.
It could be any one.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:04.701
What do you think, audience?
-Okay.

00:01:04.701 --> 00:01:06.434
What do you think? This one?
-Yeah.

00:01:06.434 --> 00:01:08.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:08.934 --> 00:01:12.167
-Alright.
-Good luck!

00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:13.467
-You feeling good?

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:14.701
-I feel good about this.
-You do?

00:01:14.701 --> 00:01:15.767
-I think so.
-Go for it, man.

00:01:15.767 --> 00:01:17.133
-You said break it here?
-Yeah.

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:19.367
-Alright, here we go.
1, 2, 3...

00:01:20.634 --> 00:01:21.934
Ooh!
-Ooh!

00:01:21.934 --> 00:01:23.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:01:25.901 --> 00:01:27.567
-Alright.

00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:30.167
We're off to a good start.

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:31.434
-That one?
-That one's a little shiny.

00:01:31.434 --> 00:01:32.567
-That's shiny.
I'm scared of that one.

00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:33.767
-I'm scared of the shiny one.

00:01:33.767 --> 00:01:36.501
I'm gonna -- That one? That one?
-Yeah, why not?

00:01:36.501 --> 00:01:37.834
-That looks cooked to me.
-Somebody said, "Why not?"

00:01:37.834 --> 00:01:39.968
-"Why not?"
-Why not?

00:01:39.968 --> 00:01:41.501
-Oh! I don't feel
good about this.

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:43.767
-Oh, this is fun.
-It's not fun.

00:01:43.767 --> 00:01:44.868
Is it fun?

00:01:44.868 --> 00:01:46.501
-Yeah. Come on.
-Are you having fun?!

00:01:46.501 --> 00:01:48.033
-Come on.

00:01:48.033 --> 00:01:49.033
Oh!

00:01:49.033 --> 00:01:50.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:01:50.033 --> 00:01:51.267
Yes.

00:01:51.267 --> 00:01:53.167
-I just squashed it so hard.
-That was amazing.

00:01:53.167 --> 00:01:54.767
-Whew!
-Alright.

00:01:54.767 --> 00:01:55.868
-That was it.
-Alright.

00:01:55.868 --> 00:01:56.934
-6-4.

00:01:56.934 --> 00:01:58.367
-That felt like it was
going to be raw.

00:01:58.367 --> 00:02:01.300
Whoa! That means there's a
lot of raw guys in there, bud.

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:03.234
[ Laughs ]
-Oh, man.

00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:04.701
Alright, I'm going to go
with this one.

00:02:04.701 --> 00:02:07.767
-Ooh! That's the biggest one.
No, I just tried that.

00:02:07.767 --> 00:02:09.167
It didn't work for me.
-It didn't work?

00:02:09.167 --> 00:02:10.334
-No.
-Alright.

00:02:10.334 --> 00:02:13.767
-Thanks for being here. Yeah.
-3, 2, 1...

00:02:13.767 --> 00:02:15.100
Ah!
-Ooh!

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:16.734
-Whoo!

00:02:16.734 --> 00:02:20.234
Alright. Alright.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:20.234 --> 00:02:22.167
-I've never --
This is the closest game --

00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:24.767
-Is this the closest?
-Yeah, we've ever played.

00:02:24.767 --> 00:02:27.067
So, these are all raw.

00:02:27.067 --> 00:02:28.234
I just -- Everyone in
the audience is going,

00:02:28.234 --> 00:02:29.267
"Yeah, why not?

00:02:29.267 --> 00:02:30.501
Just take it."
That one.

00:02:30.501 --> 00:02:31.634
Where's that shiny one?

00:02:31.634 --> 00:02:32.868
I'm not doing the shine --
No, I don't --

00:02:32.868 --> 00:02:34.234
-That's the scary one
right there.

00:02:34.234 --> 00:02:35.701
-That's the Boston Shiner.
Don't touch that.

00:02:35.701 --> 00:02:37.167
-Eh, I'll do it. I'll do it.
-Oh, my gosh!

00:02:37.167 --> 00:02:39.234
-Oh! Oh.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:39.234 --> 00:02:41.367
-I feel real good.
I say -- I feel good.

00:02:41.367 --> 00:02:42.501
I feel good.
-I feel good about this.

00:02:42.501 --> 00:02:43.667
-Yeah. Good to see you, man.

00:02:43.667 --> 00:02:44.801
I'm so happy
you came to the show.

00:02:44.801 --> 00:02:46.234
-I'm so happy to be here.
-Thanks so much.

00:02:46.234 --> 00:02:48.334
Congrats on all the success.
-Thank you so much.

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:50.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:52.067
-The shiny one.
-That's amazing.

00:02:52.067 --> 00:02:54.033
-The shiny one.
Dude, this has never happened.

00:02:54.033 --> 00:02:56.701
-This is --
-There's four raw eggs in here.

00:02:56.701 --> 00:02:59.534
-The odds are 50/50.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:02:59.534 --> 00:03:02.801
Half raw, half a-cooked.

00:03:02.801 --> 00:03:04.601
-Whoo-hoo-hoo!
-Alright.

00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:06.834
-Oh, my gosh.
-Lordy have mercy.

00:03:06.834 --> 00:03:08.167
-First one to two loses.

00:03:08.167 --> 00:03:10.367
-I'm going to go with this one.
-Alright.

00:03:10.367 --> 00:03:12.300
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:14.968 --> 00:03:17.868
What in the world
is going on?

00:03:17.868 --> 00:03:19.133
Dude.

00:03:19.133 --> 00:03:21.801
I've never ever -- This has
never -- I swear to God.

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:23.334
-Never!
-Really?

00:03:23.334 --> 00:03:25.067
-Never!
-Are any of them raw?

00:03:25.067 --> 00:03:26.367
-I cannot tell you.
-They're all hard-boiled.

00:03:26.367 --> 00:03:27.834
-This is insane.

00:03:27.834 --> 00:03:30.200
-Now the odds are
against you, James.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:34.868
-Oh, geez.
-More raw than a-cooked.

00:03:34.868 --> 00:03:36.701
Oh, hey! Hey! Oh!

00:03:36.701 --> 00:03:37.801
Pick me!"

00:03:37.801 --> 00:03:40.267
-Oh, man. Oh, man.
-Hey, why not?

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:43.000
-This can't go well --

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:45.601
-No, it's I feel -- I know
this is not going to be --

00:03:45.601 --> 00:03:48.501
